<![CDATA[<font face="Arial,Sans-Serif" size="2">Thank you for your interest in the graduate programs of the School of Earth and Space
Exploration at Arizona State University! Our innovative, interdisciplinary school currently offers
MS and PhD degrees in Astrophysics and Geological Sciences as well as a PhD in Exploration
Systems Design.
<br><br><u><b>Admission
</b></u><br>For details on our graduate programs, including program descriptions, admission requirements,
application deadlines and financial support, please visit our site <u><b>here</b></u>.
<br><br>Admission is possible for both spring and fall semesters, however spring admission is <b>very
limited</b>. To be admitted to a spring semester, a student must have an arrangement with a
faculty member who endorses her or his application and has the funding to support the student
as a research assistant.
<br><br>We strongly recommend that all applicants review our <u><b>r</b><b>esearch focus website</b></u> to identify faculty
members who share similar research interests. We encourage you to contact these faculty
members for more information regarding their research program. These connections can greatly
enhance an applicant's visibility for admission and can help identify potential research project
ideas should the applicant be admitted to our program.<br><br>Note: All of our application materials are submitted electronically. Applicants must provide all of
the required materials to be considered for admission.
<br><br><u><b>Additional Questions?</b></u>
<br>Please visit our <u><b>FAQ</b></u> page for additional information. After you have reviewed our site or
contacted prospective faculty advisors, please feel free to contact me with specific questions
about our graduate programs and the admission process.
<br><br>I hope this information is helpful. Have a great day!
<br><br>Becca Dial
<br>Academic Support Specialist
<br>School of Earth and Space Exploration
